      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While these items contain protein, you should be cautious with certain aged cheeses and cured meats when taking an MAOI. Tyramine, found in some aged foods, can interact dangerously with MAOIs, potentially causing a hypertensive crisis. For the safest approach, it's best to stick to fresh, low-tyramine sources of protein like chicken, fish, or eggs. Always check specific dietary guidelines provided by your prescribing physician.",
      "source": "target",
